# WElcome To the Festive Season

Welcome to the Festive Season! We kicked off November with some fantastic workshops with Epzio Bangoura. Both drumming and dancing  workshops with Epizo were awesome with his thorough step by step breakdowns of routines and rhythms. Not to mention his fabulous humor and incredible kora playing skills at the evening concert! A huge thank you to Natalie Richy for once again delivering such a well organised and heart-felt event. Yay! This month we are really focusing on what 2015 brings for us and you as students, clients and rhythm junkies out there! Excitingly we are introducing a new beginners class which begins in just two weeks, along with a drum making workshop to get you all prepared for the festivals and 2015 classes up ahead! We are also doing a call out to those of you that would like to enrol your child into Rhythm Culture kids classes for next year. For students, we want to remind you of upcoming performances in November and December which you can ask Nathaniel about in class. There are six more weeks of classes before we have a break over the Christmas holidays so make sure to come and get your healthy dose of rhythm. Have a fantastic month!
